    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 403,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#biomes",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**Spike-prove the shared-runtime assumption \u2014 HOLDS** (2026-07-27, `tools/spikes/biomes/`, memo at `MEMO.md`, `run.sh` re-runs it). **16/16 checks across three build shapes, four of them against a shape that MUST fail** \u2014 a suite that has never said no is not evidence. **Shape A** (one Vite build, three biomes \u2014 the Phase 3 flip): one runtime, one shared-store instance, a store written in biome A observed in biome B, all mounted from plain HTML with no SvelteKit. Identity, not resemblance \u2014 each biome hands the page its own reference to Svelte's scheduler and the page compares them. **Shape B** (three independent builds, the CONTROL): three runtimes, no sharing, and the probe detects all of it. **Shape C** (a biome built LATER, borrowing the host runtime by URL \u2014 the ui-Sprig case): 1.6 kB, shares both. **Three costs the plan had not priced.** (1) \"Externalise the runtime\" is not one specifier \u2014 marking `svelte/internal` external and leaving `svelte` alone builds clean and throws `Function called outside component initialization` at mount; in a marketplace that fails in someone else's deployment after graft. (2) Publishing the runtime defeats tree-shaking: 27.3 kB \u2192 95.4 kB unminified. Phase 3 does not pay it; the Sprig marketplace does, after which each late biome costs 1.6 kB. (3) Vite's default `preserveEntrySignatures: false` ships mangled export names, unusable as an interface. All three are one shape \u2014 the host must publish a deliberate interface, and every default is against it. Also measured: a biome is a CSS boundary, and `shadow: 'none'` removes the boundary and the encapsulation together. The `$app/*` surface is 64 of 317 components and nine symbols, `goto`+`page` being 80 of 81 sites, shimmed in ~50 lines. **What it does NOT say**: no biome was put on a page beside the legacy SvelteKit bundle, and these biomes are toys \u2014 the chat core's 710 handlers and 859 bindings are untested. Phase 4 unblocked on runtime grounds."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 404,
          "tags": [
            "#sprigs",
            "#ui"
          ],
          "text": "Write costs (1) and (2) above into the ui-Sprig spec \u2014 they are the MECHANISM behind \"no framework sprigs\", not a matter of taste"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 405,
          "tags": [
            "#perf",
            "#bonsai"
          ],
          "text": "**Version `/themes/active.css` once the shell is server-rendered** (deferred here from the 2026-07-26 caching pass. **That premise is now false and the item is NOT blocked**: the panels moved to Jinja2 on 2026-08-01 but `shell.py` deliberately did not \u2014 it interpolates three escaped values against four raw ones, so a template would need four `| safe`, which is the hatch autoescape exists to avoid. Nothing here needs templating anyway: `shell.asset_url()` already version-stamps by release, and this wants the same treatment plus an ETag). MEASURED on the shipped image with no theme grafted \u2014 the common case: `HTTP 200`, `cache-control: no-cache`, **no ETag, no Last-Modified**, and a conditional request with `If-None-Match` still returns **200, not 304**. So every full page load spends a render-blocking round-trip on 23 bytes of `/* no theme grafted */`, via the static `<link>` at `app.html:21`. Do NOT invalidate this on image/container updates: `SPRIG_ACTIVE_THEME` is flipped by a graft and cleared by a prune at RUNTIME (`routers/sprigs.py:151,305`) with no restart, so deploy-keyed invalidation would leave an operator's freshly grafted theme invisible until restart \u2014 the exact failure the Sprig durability work exists to prevent. Right design: inject `?v=<active theme name + css mtime>` into the shell's `<link>` at serve time, then serve the CSS `immutable, max-age=31536000`. A graft changes the token, so the URL changes, so pickup is instant AND there is zero revalidation in between (same trick SvelteKit uses for `_app/immutable`). Interim options considered and rejected for now: a short TTL (a grafted theme could appear one load late) and an ETag-only fix (saves a 23-byte body, not the round-trip)."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "773a17407668c198",
      "line_num": 402,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#frontend"
      ],
      "text": "**Phase S \u2014 streaming spike: GO, with two conditions (2026-07-27, `tools/spikes/streaming/`, memo at `MEMO.md`). All four done-criteria measured, not asserted: HTTP/2 (`http_version 2` on shell, island and vendored htmx, via Caddy `flush_interval -1` \u2014 without that line the proxy buffers and the spike looks fine while proving nothing); incremental delivery (frame 1 at 0.000 s \u2192 frame 150 at 3.337 s); stop really stops \u2014 client `{outcome:\"stopped\", tokens:219/453}` AND server `stream_aborted sent=21 total=164`, which is the half that matters, since a stop button that only hides output is theatre; autoscroll holds. 8/8 under Playwright, TTFT 5 ms, ~260 lines of stdlib server + framework-free island. Two findings that change the plan. (1) Cypress cannot see streaming \u2014 it MITM-proxies the AUT and buffers the body, so the page observes nothing until the stream ends. Not fixable with better assertions; any streaming guard-rail needs a non-proxying driver. (2) Autoscroll took four attempts, and attempt 3 passed every automated check while being broken on real hardware \u2014 inferring intent from gesture deltas went 13/13 green under Playwright and released the pin on PAGE LOAD, from trackpad jitter. Shipped: judge by POSITION on every scroll event, plus a rule refusing to yank a reader who has moved the box. No gesture listeners at all, so momentum, scrollbar drag and keyboard paging come free. GO is conditional: a non-proxying driver lands before any streaming surface is cut \u2014 necessary but NOT sufficient, since attempt 3 was green under exactly such a driver \u2014 so every streamed surface needs a human pass before it is called done. Phase 4 stays gated on the shared-runtime probe; this spike tested vanilla streaming, which needs no runtime at all.**\n- [x] **Spike-prove the shared-runtime assumption \u2014 HOLDS** (2026-07-27, `tools/spikes/biomes/`, memo at `MEMO.md`, `run.sh` re-runs it). **16/16 checks across three build shapes, four of them against a shape that MUST fail** \u2014 a suite that has never said no is not evidence. **Shape A** (one Vite build, three biomes \u2014 the Phase 3 flip): one runtime, one shared-store instance, a store written in biome A observed in biome B, all mounted from plain HTML with no SvelteKit. Identity, not resemblance \u2014 each biome hands the page its own reference to Svelte's scheduler and the page compares them. **Shape B** (three independent builds, the CONTROL): three runtimes, no sharing, and the probe detects all of it. **Shape C** (a biome built LATER, borrowing the host runtime by URL \u2014 the ui-Sprig case): 1.6 kB, shares both. **Three costs the plan had not priced.** (1) \"Externalise the runtime\" is not one specifier \u2014 marking `svelte/internal` external and leaving `svelte` alone builds clean and throws `Function called outside component initialization` at mount; in a marketplace that fails in someone else's deployment after graft. (2) Publishing the runtime defeats tree-shaking: 27.3 kB \u2192 95.4 kB unminified. Phase 3 does not pay it; the Sprig marketplace does, after which each late biome costs 1.6 kB. (3) Vite's default `preserveEntrySignatures: false` ships mangled export names, unusable as an interface. All three are one shape \u2014 the host must publish a deliberate interface, and every default is against it. Also measured: a biome is a CSS boundary, and `shadow: 'none'` removes the boundary and the encapsulation together. The `$app/*` surface is 64 of 317 components and nine symbols, `goto`+`page` being 80 of 81 sites, shimmed in ~50 lines. **What it does NOT say**: no biome was put on a page beside the legacy SvelteKit bundle, and these biomes are toys \u2014 the chat core's 710 handlers and 859 bindings are untested. Phase 4 unblocked on runtime grounds. #frontend #biomes #critical\n- [ ] Write costs (1) and (2) above into the ui-Sprig spec \u2014 they are the MECHANISM behind \"no framework sprigs\", not a matter of taste #sprigs #ui\n- [ ] **Version `/themes/active.css` once the shell is server-rendered** (deferred here from the 2026-07-26 caching pass. **That premise is now false and the item is NOT blocked**: the panels moved to Jinja2 on 2026-08-01 but `shell.py` deliberately did not \u2014 it interpolates three escaped values against four raw ones, so a template would need four `| safe`, which is the hatch autoescape exists to avoid. Nothing here needs templating anyway: `shell.asset_url()` already version-stamps by release, and this wants the same treatment plus an ETag). MEASURED on the shipped image with no theme grafted \u2014 the common case: `HTTP 200`, `cache-control: no-cache`, **no ETag, no Last-Modified**, and a conditional request with `If-None-Match` still returns **200, not 304**. So every full page load spends a render-blocking round-trip on 23 bytes of `/* no theme grafted */`, via the static `<link>` at `app.html:21`. Do NOT invalidate this on image/container updates: `SPRIG_ACTIVE_THEME` is flipped by a graft and cleared by a prune at RUNTIME (`routers/sprigs.py:151,305`) with no restart, so deploy-keyed invalidation would leave an operator's freshly grafted theme invisible until restart \u2014 the exact failure the Sprig durability work exists to prevent. Right design: inject `?v=<active theme name + css mtime>` into the shell's `<link>` at serve time, then serve the CSS `immutable, max-age=31536000`. A graft changes the token, so the URL changes, so pickup is instant AND there is zero revalidation in between (same trick SvelteKit uses for `_app/immutable`). Interim options considered and rejected for now: a short TTL (a grafted theme could appear one load late) and an ETag-only fix (saves a 23-byte body, not the round-trip). #perf #bonsai\n\n`#frontend`\n`TODO.md:L402`",
